```text
class Animal:
    method makeSound():
        print("...")

class Dog extends Animal:
    method makeSound():           // overrides Animal.makeSound
        print("Woof")

class Cat extends Animal:
    method makeSound():           // overrides Animal.makeSound
        print("Meow")

class Cow extends Animal:
    method makeSound():           // overrides Animal.makeSound
        print("Moo")

animals: List<Animal> = [new Dog(), new Cat(), new Cow()]

for animal in animals:
    animal.makeSound()            // same call, different output each time

// Output:
// Woof
// Meow
// Moo
```

The loop calls `makeSound()` through the `Animal` type every time. Dynamic dispatch picks each object's own version — the loop never checks what kind of animal it has.
